The way forward is to look a lot at existing Moodle code and see how things are done there. The particular problem you are facing is that you have the course module id and now need the course module object itself. Look at the beginning of view.php how it does it: 
```text
if (! $cm = get_record("course_modules", "id", $id)) {


            error("Course Module ID was incorrect");


        }
```
 After that the variable $cm will hold the course module object or you will have received an error message.
